gulatory circuit in butterfly eyespot evolution</article-title><source>Science</source><volume>283</volume><fpage>532</fpage><lpage>534</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9915699</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pbio-1000037-b012"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Monteiro</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Glaser</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Stockslagger</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Glansdorp</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Ramos</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Comparative insights into questions of lepidopteran wing pattern homology</article-title><source>BMC Dev Biol</source><volume>6</volume><fpage>52</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17090321</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pbio-1000037-b013"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>PN</given-names></name><name><surname>Callaerts</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>De Couet</surname><given-names>HG</given-names></name><name><surname>Martindale</surname><given-names>MQ</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Cephalopod <italic>Hox</italic> genes and the origin of morphological novelties</article-title><source>Nature</source><volume>424</volume><fpage>1061</fpage><lpage>1065</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12944969</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pbio-1000037-b014"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Jockusch</surname><given-names>EL</given-names></name><name><surname>Ober</surname><given-names>KA</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Hypothesis testing in evolutionary developmental biology: A case study from insect wings</article-title><source>J Heredity</source><volume>95</volume><fpage>382</fpage><lpage>396</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pbio-1000037-b015"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Panganiban</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Nagy</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Carroll</surname><given-names>SB</given-names></name></person-group><year>1994</year><article-title>The role of the <italic>Distal-less</italic> gene in the development and evolution of insect limbs</article-title><source>Curr Biol</source><volume>4</volume><fpage>671</fpage><lpage>675</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7953552</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pbio-1000037-b016"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Brakefield</surname><given-names>PM</given-names></name><name><surname>Gates</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Keys</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Kesbeke</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Wijngaarden</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>Development, plasticity and evolution of butterfly eyespot patterns</article-title><source>Nature</source><volume>384</volume><fpage>236</fpage><lpage>242</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12809139</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pbio-1000037-b017"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Gorfinkiel</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Morata</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Guerrero</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>The homeobox gene <italic>Distal-less</italic> induces ventral appendage development in <named-content content-type="genus-species">Drosophila</named-content></article-title><source>Genes Dev</source><volume>11</volume><fpage>2259</fpage><lpage>2271</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9303541</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pbio-1000037-b018"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Dong</surname><given-names>PDS</given-names></name><name><surname>Dicks</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name><name><surname>Panganiban</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title><italic>Distal-less</italic> and <italic>homothorax</italic> regulate multiple targets to pattern the <named-content content-type="genus-species">Drosophila</named-content> antenna</article-title><source>Development</source><volume>129</volume><fpage>1967</fpage><lpage>1974</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11934862</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pbio-1000037-b019"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Brunetti</surname><given-names>CR</given-names></name><name><surname>Selegue</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name><name><surname>Monteiro</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>French</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Brakefield</surname><given-names>PM</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>The generation and diversification of butterfly eyespot color patterns</article-title><source>Curr Biol</source><volume>11</volume><fpage>1578</fpage><lpage>1585</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11676917</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pbio-1000037-b020"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group><name><surname>Schlosser</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>The role of modules in development and evolution</article-title><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Schlosser</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Wagner</surname><given-names>GP</given-names></name></person-group><comment>editors</comment><source>Modularity in development and evolution</source><publisher-loc>Chicago</publisher-loc><publisher-name>University of Chicago Press</publisher-name><fpage>519</fpage><lpage>582</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pbio-1000037-b021"><citation citation-type="journal"><